input.pseudocode:
// NOTATION for the evidence table: arg/output are shown with C-style escapes for
// non-printable bytes (\t=0x09, \n=0x0A, \v=0x0B, \f=0x0C, \r=0x0D, \xNN otherwise).
// All other characters are literal bytes. Outputs are the byte-exact contents of
// physical line 10 (excluding its terminating '\n'), captured with `od -c`.

FUNCTION parameterize(s: byte string, sep: byte string = "-") -> byte string:
    // Pure, single-pass, context-free per-byte map. No state, no lookahead,
    // no collapsing, no trimming, no normalization, no transliteration.
    result = ""                       // empty byte string
    FOR i = 0 TO length(s) - 1:
        c = s[i]                      // one raw byte, 0x01..0xFF
        IF c IS IN 'a'..'z' (0x61..0x7A) OR c IS IN '0'..'9' (0x30..0x39):
            append byte c to result                 // kept verbatim
        ELSE IF c IS IN 'A'..'Z' (0x41..0x5A):
            append byte (c + 0x20) to result        // ASCII-lowercased
        ELSE IF c == ' ' (0x20):
            append sep to result                    // exactly one separator per space
        ELSE:
            /* emit nothing — the byte is DELETED */
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN result                     // returned as-is: NOT squeezed, NOT stripped

// Equivalent one-liner:  result = concat over bytes b of s of
//     ascii_tolower(b) if ascii_isalnum(b) else sep if b == 0x20 else ""

// CONFIRMED PROPERTIES (each backed by probes below):
//  P1. The separator is emitted for byte 0x20 ONLY. All other C `isspace` bytes
//      — 0x09 TAB, 0x0A LF, 0x0B VT, 0x0C FF, 0x0D CR — are DELETED, exactly like
//      punctuation. => The reconnaissance hypothesis "else if it is whitespace"
//      is REFUTED; the correct predicate is `c == ' '`.
//  P2. Runs of separators are NOT collapsed/squeezed. N consecutive spaces yield
//      exactly N separator characters (verified up to N = 10 and in fuzzing).
//      Non-collapsing also holds ACROSS the template boundary: W=" lead" gives
//      "the--lead-test" (the space ending "The " and the leading space of W each
//      produce their own '-').
//  P3. Non-space bytes deleted from between two spaces do not merge them:
//      W="-a-" -> "the-a-test" but W=" -a- " -> "the--a--test".
//  P4. ASCII digits 0x30..0x39 are KEPT. Underscore 0x5F is DELETED (this is the
//      main divergence from Rails, which keeps '_'). Hyphen 0x2D is DELETED too
//      (so an already-parameterized string is NOT idempotent under this function).
//  P5. All high bytes 0x80..0xFF are DELETED unconditionally. Therefore every
//      non-ASCII UTF-8 character vanishes completely (2-, 3- and 4-byte
//      sequences alike): "café"->"caf", "naïve"->"nave", "ÄÖÜ"->"", "中文"->"",
//      U+1F600 -> "", NBSP (C2 A0) -> "", "€5" -> "5".
//  P6. All control bytes 0x01..0x1F and 0x7F are DELETED.
//  P7. Behavior is LOCALE-INDEPENDENT: identical output under LC_ALL=C,
//      C.UTF-8, en_US.UTF-8, tr_TR.UTF-8, en_US.ISO-8859-1. So the alnum/lower
//      tests are ASCII-hardcoded (or setlocale is never called). In particular
//      'I' -> 'i' even under tr_TR, and Latin-1 byte 0xC9 is dropped under
//      ISO-8859-1.
//  P8. No length limit / no truncation: verified with |W| = 1000, 10000 and
//      100000; output length matched the model exactly (809 / 8009 / 80009).
//  P9. The empty string maps to the empty string: W="" -> "the--test", i.e.
//      parameterize("The  Test") = "the" + "-" + "" + "-" + "test".

// VALIDATION: an exhaustive single-byte scan of W = "q" <b> "z" for every
// b in 0x01..0xFF (255 probes) produced exactly the map above, and 4 randomized
// fuzz campaigns (~2400 probes: random bytes, punctuation-heavy alphabet,
// space-heavy alphabet, lengths 0..1000) reported 0 mismatches against this
// pseudocode.
